<title>FINLAND: VALMET SAYS SIGNS PORSCHE DEAL.</title>
<headline>VALMET SAYS SIGNS PORSCHE DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish paper machinery maker Valmet Oy said on Tuesday its automotive unit had sealed an earlier announced deal with German car maker Porsche AG to build over 5,000 Porsche sportscars per year.</p>
<p>The companies announced the plans to build Porsche Boxsters at Valmet's Uusikaupunki, Finland, plant in January, and serial production will begin in September, Valmet said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
